

1. Virtual DOM
The Virtual DOM is a JavaScript representation of the UI.
Virtual DOM is an in-memory representation of the UI. React uses it to determine what has changed between renders and then applies the necessary changes to the real DOM."

2. Reconciliation
During reconciliation, React determines the changes between the previous and next render trees. The commit phase then applies the required DOM mutations

3. React Fiber
React Fiber is React's internal reconciliation architecture. It breaks rendering work into units that React can schedule and prioritize, which enables features such as interruptible rendering and concurrent capabilities.

4.Render Phase	                             Commit Phase
Determines what should change	                 Applies changes
Reconciliation happens	                       DOM mutations happen
Can be interrupted/restarted	                 Must be completed consistently
Should be pure	                               Performs side effects/DOM mutations

